TABLE OF CONTENTS

usbclass/USBClassBind
usbclass/USBClassUnbind
usbclass/USBClassBind                                    usbclass/USBClassBind

   NAME
	USBClassBind -- An interface offered: true if the driver takes it - it has opened its pipes and filled a unit, `binding.unit` saying which - false if it declines and the next driver is asked.

   SYNOPSIS
	    bool USBClassBind(*usb.USBBinding binding)

   BEHAVIOR
	Called on the bus's process, which nothing else on the bus moves while
	it runs: decide quickly, and leave anything slow to the driver's own
	task. It may make control transfers on the device (DoUSBControl) and
	open pipes.
usbclass/USBClassUnbind                                usbclass/USBClassUnbind

   NAME
	USBClassUnbind -- The interface is gone - the device was pulled, or the bus stops: every request the driver has outstanding on it answered, its pipes closed, its unit left without what was in it.

   SYNOPSIS
	    void USBClassUnbind(*usb.USBBinding binding)

   BEHAVIOR
	Called on the bus's process.
